      "kind": "antiskill",
      "text": "Do not assume that bound evaluation inside the forward light cone implies metric correctness. The LR bound is a one-sided envelope, not a metric derivation."
    },
    {
      "kind": "skill",
      "text": "Compute exact rational envelope values by keeping C_a, mu_a, a, v_hop(a) as symbolic rationals. For the fixture c=1,t=1,x=(1,1), the bound evaluates to 1/4 exactly when dilation factor=2 and mu_a=1."
    },
    {
      "kind": "antibody",
      "text": "Antiskill: Do not promote LR bound evaluation as proof of Minkowski metric or its scale. The bound is consistent with multiple metric signatures given appropriate parameter choices."
    }
  ]
